            <ArticleTitle>Coronary calcium as a reliable tool for differentiating ischemic from nonischemic cardiomyopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>191-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In conclusion, the presence or absence of coronary calcium as detected by this rapid technique represents a simple and reliable noninvasive sign for the differential diagnosis between ischemic and nonischemic DC.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
